From: RabbizOS developers
Subject: arm64: dts: exynos: a217f: limit gadget speed during USB bring-up

High-speed repeatedly loses the link on the test Mac (67-78 losses/minute).
Disabling USB2 LPM and PHY suspend did not resolve it. Full-speed is a
connectivity workaround; the high-speed failure remains under investigation.
See docs/a21s-usb-flapping.md for controlled measurements and limitations.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos850-a217f.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos850-a217f.dts
@@ -534,4 +534,4 @@
 &usbdrd_dwc3 {
 	dr_mode = "otg";
-	maximum-speed = "high-speed";
+	maximum-speed = "full-speed";
 };
